                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="14XX" notBefore="1400" notAfter="1499" calendar="#gregorian">s. xv</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#d m" source="2612"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_198">Eton,
                        Buckinghamshire. Royal College of the Assumption of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Identifiable in the inventory of 1465 (SC229), confirmed by
                        second folio. The manuscript also contains marginalia in the hand of Robert
                        Elyot (d. 1499), fellow of Eton from c. 1474 until his death in January 1499
                        (BRUO 638). He was a prolific annotator of books at Eton. Five are
                        particularly heavily marked and were probably his own, subsequently given to
                        the college: MSS 17, 18, 34, 36, 76. (His marks were discussed by N. R. Ker
                        in The Library, 5th ser. 30 (1975), 233--7, with an addendum by R. Beadle in
                        The Library, 5th ser. 32 (1977), 371--2.)</p><p>(Medieval binding. Large
                        12-nail label now missing from lower cover.)</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Formerly at St Albans (q.v.), given by Abbot
                     John Whethamstede (abbot, 1420--40 and 1451--65).</provenance>
               <provenance type="#e" source="4830"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_474">St Albans,
                        Hertfordshire. Benedictine abbey of St Alban</orgName><p>At end: 'Hunc
                        librum ad usum Conuentus Monasterii sancti Albani assignauit venerabilis
                        pater dompnus Iohannes Whethamstede olim Abbas Monasterii antedicti,
                        vinculoque anathematis innodauit illos omnes qui aut titulum illius delere
                        curauerint aut ad usus applicare presumpserint alienos'.</p><p>Shortly
                        afterwards (by 1465) acquired by Eton College (q.v.).</p></provenance>
                  </history>
